title "Deploy, then plan without touching anything: the deployment stamp must not show as drift"
trace $CLI bundle deploy

# Only the deploy phase stamps deployment.deployment_id (it is not known until the
# version is claimed), so plan sees it in the state and in the workspace but not in the
# local config. Without an ignore_local_changes rule that absence plans an update on a
# job and a pipeline nobody edited.
trace $CLI bundle plan | contains.py "Plan: 0 to add, 0 to change, 0 to delete, 2 unchanged"

title "A second deploy is a no-op too: no update request for either resource"
trace $CLI bundle deploy
trace print_requests.py //api/2.2/jobs //api/2.0/pipelines --sort
